The separate staged request-body envelope package at
`target/parliament-request-family-envelope-publication-stage/publication` covers
body shape bounds. Since `R` depends only on row, role and `M`, its H/CX and
retained-purifier additions are constant across each admitted public-shape family.
They therefore preserve those bodies' shape-maximizing witnesses conditionally.
This observation is not a family-wide quantum/adaptive theorem or a complete
experiment bound. The wrapper's broader unknown-resource flag remains false.

`capture.py` restores archived component sources and current wrapper inputs into
a separate execution tree, runs the31 tests and the observer there, compares the
exact ordered test membership with its authenticated preliminary receipt, and
checks selected snapshots, execution files and loaded repository module hashes.
The loose observation and preliminary test capture are retained separately;
the final capture does not silently equate them with a new execution. Initial
observer, test-helper and README bytes are preserved in `preliminary-sources`.
